{
 "ep": 26,
 "total": 140,
 "title": "Extensions: Install, Create and Manage",
 "phase": "Installation & Administration",
 "lines": [
  {
   "say": "PostgreSQL extensions: plug-ins for your database.",
   "cap": "PostgreSQL extensions: *plug-ins* for your database."
  },
  {
   "say": "This is episode twenty six of the PostgreSQL DBA series. Today: installing and managing extensions.",
   "cap": "Episode 26: *install, create, manage.*",
   "cue": "installing"
  },
  {
   "say": "An extension is a package of SQL objects, like functions, data types and operators, managed as one unit.",
   "cap": "An *extension* = SQL objects managed as *one unit.*",
   "cue": "package"
  },
  {
   "say": "On disk, it is a control file plus SQL scripts.",
   "cap": "A *control file* plus *SQL scripts.*",
   "cue": "control"
  },
  {
   "say": "Many also ship a shared library of C code.",
   "cap": "Often a *shared library* of C code.",
   "cue": "library"
  },
  {
   "say": "Key idea: available is not the same as installed.",
   "cap": "*Available* is not *installed.*",
   "cue": "available"
  },
  {
   "say": "Step one: the extension's files are installed on the server, for example from operating system packages.",
   "cap": "Step 1: *files on the server.*",
   "cue": "server"
  },
  {
   "say": "Step two: CREATE EXTENSION loads it into the current database only.",
   "cap": "Step 2: *CREATE EXTENSION* in *one database.*",
   "cue": "CREATE"
  },
  {
   "say": "The view pg_available_extensions shows what the server offers.",
   "cap": "*pg_available_extensions:* what the server offers.",
   "cue": "offers"
  },
  {
   "say": "installed_version stays empty until CREATE EXTENSION runs in this database.",
   "cap": "*installed_version* empty = *not created yet.*",
   "cue": "empty"
  },
  {
   "say": "In psql, backslash dx lists what this database has. Output trimmed.",
   "cap": "*\\dx* lists installed extensions.",
   "cue": "lists"
  },
  {
   "say": "Who can create one? Usually only a superuser.",
   "cap": "Usually: *superuser only.*",
   "cue": "superuser"
  },
  {
   "say": "But trusted extensions, like pg_trgm and pgcrypto, need only CREATE privilege on the database.",
   "cap": "*Trusted:* CREATE on the database is enough.",
   "cue": "trusted"
  },
  {
   "say": "As app_user, pg_trgm worked.",
   "cap": "app_user: *pg_trgm worked.*",
   "cue": "worked"
  },
  {
   "say": "dblink is not trusted, so: permission denied to create extension.",
   "cap": "dblink: *permission denied.*",
   "cue": "permission"
  },
  {
   "say": "Files missing on the server? The error is: extension is not available.",
   "cap": "Missing files: *not available.*",
   "cue": "error"
  },
  {
   "say": "Versions are per database. Here pg_trgm one point five is installed, and the default is one point six.",
   "cap": "Installed *1.5,* default *1.6.*",
   "cue": "default"
  },
  {
   "say": "ALTER EXTENSION pg_trgm UPDATE moves it up. Run it again: already installed.",
   "cap": "*ALTER EXTENSION ... UPDATE*",
   "cue": "again"
  },
  {
   "say": "With a pg_trgm index in place, DROP EXTENSION is refused.",
   "cap": "Dependent index: *DROP is refused.*",
   "cue": "refused"
  },
  {
   "say": "CASCADE would drop that index too, so read the detail first.",
   "cap": "*CASCADE* drops the *dependents* too.",
   "cue": "detail"
  },
  {
   "say": "pg_stat_statements must be listed in shared_preload_libraries, which needs a server restart.",
   "cap": "*shared_preload_libraries* = *restart.*",
   "cue": "restart"
  },
  {
   "say": "Without it, CREATE EXTENSION works, but the view fails: must be loaded via shared_preload_libraries.",
   "cap": "Created, but *not loaded.*",
   "cue": "fails"
  },
  {
   "say": "pg_dump writes only the CREATE EXTENSION command, so the restore server needs the same files.",
   "cap": "*pg_dump:* only *CREATE EXTENSION.*",
   "cue": "files"
  },
  {
   "say": "A common rollout practice: test in staging, pin the version, use migrations, and check every database.",
   "cap": "Rollout: *staging,* *pin version,* *migrations.*",
   "cue": "pin"
  },
  {
   "say": "Recap: files on the server, CREATE EXTENSION per database, trusted or superuser, and ALTER EXTENSION UPDATE.",
   "cap": "Recap: *available,* *created,* *updated.*",
   "cue": "trusted"
  },
  {
   "say": "Next up: useful PostgreSQL catalogs and the information schema. Follow so you don't miss it, and send this to a friend who's learning PostgreSQL.",
   "cap": "Next up: *catalogs.* *Follow* and share."
  }
 ],
